# Queue: one follow-up typed and submitted while a turn is busy. It does
# not start a second turn (internal/tui/app.go's handleSubmit: m.busy &&
# !m.prompt.Active()) — it commits right away as a "you" block with a
# "queued" meta (internal/tui/transcript.go's RenderUserMessageMeta) and
# the busy line grows a " · 1 queued" suffix (transcript.go's
# RenderSpinnerLeft, driven by harness/lane.go Steer's EventQueueUpdate).
@faux testdata/faux/qa/queue-busy.yaml
@size 120x40

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
SHOT welcome
TYPE start the rate limiter work
KEY enter
WAITFOR /esc to stop/ 10
SHOT busy
TYPE also check the login route
KEY enter
SHOT queued-one
EXPECT /1 queued/
EXPECT /you/
EXPECT /queued/
EXPECT /also check the login route/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
WAITFOR /Checked the login route/ 30
SHOT drained
EXPECT_NOT /[0-9] queued/
